# Hephaestus

Delivery runs a fixed loop — orient, plan, critique, implement, review, test, ship, finish. Slash commands in `.cursor/commands/` drive it; the subagents in `.cursor/agents/` absorb the verbose work. Quality gates, retry limits, and autonomy rules live in `CLAUDE.md` — read it there rather than assuming.

## Chains

A command that chains another must load that command's file and follow it — never paraphrase it from memory.

| Command | Chains |
| --- | --- |
| /autopilot | /start-issue, /ship, /finish |
| /finish | /update-docs |
| /orient | /worktrees |
| /refactor | /ship, /finish |
| /ship | /critique |
| /start-issue | /test-issue |

## Cursor mapping

- **Subagents, no worktrees.** Under Claude Code the `coder` agent runs in an isolated git worktree. Cursor subagents share one working tree — serialize file-modifying tasks.
- **Least privilege is only partly enforced.** `researcher`, `reviewer`, and `explorer` carry `readonly: true`, which sandboxes their shell — shell writes fail. It does not withhold the write tools, and those bypass the sandbox, so file writes still rest on instruction. `tester` is exempt: its shell must write for tests to run. `tools:` is prose to Cursor, not an access control.
- **Commands are injected verbatim.** Cursor strips YAML frontmatter only from imported `.claude/commands` files, so these adapters carry none. `$ARGUMENTS` and `$1`… are substituted.
- **Never hand-edit `.cursor/`.** Edit `.ai/workflows/` and `.claude/agents/` in the hephaestus clone, then run `scripts/sync-cursor-adapters.sh`.
